      "headline": "NO CURSE IN THE OLDEST STORY",
      "text": "In one of the oldest accounts of Medusa, there is no curse. Around 700 BC, the poet Hesiod says she is simply born a Gorgon, the only mortal one of three sisters. The beautiful young woman whose hair became snakes comes later, from the Roman poet Ovid.",
